WEBVTT

00:01:28.924 --> 00:01:29.924
I can manage now.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.140
You better keep their eyes open.

00:01:31.564 --> 00:01:32.044
All right, Jake.

00:01:32.844 --> 00:01:34.384
I'll go up on the cliff and take a look around.

00:01:50.508 --> 00:01:51.508
Here comes Gordon!

00:02:07.292 --> 00:02:07.612
Gordon.

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:58.740
inside there was me.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.000
Catch it up.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.940
that explosion the same men who attacked you before your gold mine isn't a secret any longer

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:13.720
zeke the sooner you get your claim filed the better gold strike at harper's creek many new

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:20.130
settlers arriving in order to keep outlaws from attacking these newcomers our citizens are

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:25.410
organizing a mount of patrol members of this patrol will assemble in town this afternoon

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:29.900
following which they will ride out to meet a wagon train reported arriving from

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.680
Gold strike would bring people in here by the thousands.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.520
Settlers whose boats are sure to be for statehood.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:40.960
If we don't find a way to stop them, we're going to lose control of this territory.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.280
It ain't so easy to stop a gold rush.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.270
We can only destroy that first wagon train that's coming in.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:48.280
That would discourage others from following.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:51.810
Sure it would, but what about the posse that's riding out to bring the wagons in?

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:52.830
We can't buck them.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:54.670
They haven't got a stop yet, Baxter.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:58.400
The posse is going to use the marshal's office for headquarters.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:04:59.920
Here's what I want you to do.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.290
You select one of your best men, a man you can depend upon.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:07.520
Every able-bodied man in town is ready to ride with us to meet the wagon train.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:11.020
Well, I'm mighty proud of the spirit, Creston City, you showing.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:11.840
Wonderful.

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:15.270
Dick Gordon is out organizing a second patrol among the ranchers.

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:17.590
A group of riders will be ready in any emergency.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:19.490
He'll be here soon to join us.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:21.040
Well, now we're getting somewhere.

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.150
Is the marshal here?

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:27.100
I'm the marshal.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:28.000
What's your trouble?

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.920
My wagon train needs help, or it'll be wiped.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:41.310
out. It's hit. Now, here, the wagon train from Kansas. They stopped just across the border to

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:47.980
water up. Me and three other men rode on ahead. In Miller's Gap, we was ambushed by outlaws. I'm

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:53.110
the only one that got through a line. Outlaws? An ambush? The wagons will be coming through any

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:58.340
time now. They've got to be saved. Miller's Gap? That's a lot farther out than we planned on

00:05:58.340 --> 00:05:59.980
meeting them. I'll get the posse started.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.240
You stay here and take it easy till I get back.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:03.980
I'll get the princess for an extradition.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:04.340
What?

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:17.400
Nice, huh?

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:19.740
Faith, you almost convinced me.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:21.800
Well, this is perfect.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:24.550
Marshall and his men riding toward the gap.

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:27.410
Baxter and his men can be destroying those wagons in Dixie Canyon.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:29.040
Yeah, I'd better be on my way.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:29.980
No, that'll look...

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:33.000
Suspicious. You stick around until the marshal gets through questioning him.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.200
Then get out of town fast.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:35.260
You bet I will.

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.850
I just saw the posse riding out. What's up?

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:47.810
They're going to surprise some outlaws at Miller's Gap.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:49.150
Get the press ready, Ten Point.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:50.990
I'll have a story to print when I come back.

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:53.410
Miss Barbara, you don't need to go out there.

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:55.090
There's one roundup I'm not going to miss.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:13.110
feeling better now yeah i was sort of tuckered out i reckon that better be on my way oh stick

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:20.320
around till the posse gets here i can't do that why not well i i want to be in all this crap with

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:25.680
those outlaws oh let the posse take care of them i want you here to identify any prisoners they

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:29.650
bring in i'll be back in time for that you're not leaving i tell you

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:29.750
We'll be right back.

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:31.280
You mean I can't go?

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:33.160
You can put it any way you want.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:37.160
You got some special reason for leaving?

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:39.250
I got a reason.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:40.930
Get your hands up.

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:45.470
The reason I can't wait for that posse is that I sent them the wrong way,

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:47.850
so those wagons could be knocked off in Dixie Canyon.

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:49.390
Why, you mangy coyote?

00:07:49.390 --> 00:07:50.210
Shut up, you're lit.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:51.710
Get in that cell.

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:28.230
in a drawer.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:39.700
This man came in here with a faked-up story that sent the posse on the wrong trail.

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:43.280
His pals are all set to attack the wagon train in Dixie Canyon.

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:44.630
Where's the posse heading for?

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:45.490
Miller's Gap.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:47.280
I'll head for the wagons and warn them.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.040
You better send someone to turn the posse.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:51.120
Yeah, but there ain't a neighbor-bodied man left here.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:52.720
And I can't leave town.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:54.490
Ten points at the Herald Office.

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:54.930
Send him.

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:56.560
Ten points.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:08:59.920
Tell you the story was a fake.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:02.580
I'm waiting for those wagons near Dixie Canyon.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:04.000
Are you sure?

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.080
Half yet, the marshal told me himself.

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:07.990
I'm riding out to overtake the puss.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:09.200
Well, then get started.

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:10.450
I'll head for Dixie Canyon.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.920
Set up, men. As soon as the wagons come in sight, we'll attack.

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:48.600
Force them off on that side road.

00:09:48.990 --> 00:09:50.230
That'll drive them into the canyon.

00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:52.770
Right. Pete and Dirk are set to blow up the canyon road,

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:54.190
and we'll catch them like rats in a trap.

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:06.770
Get those horses unhitched.

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:08.410
We'll have to roll the wagon to the edge.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:01.220
Thank you.

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:00.460
Thank you.
